---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE, pathFor } from '../../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title="Ceiling Fan Transition AI vs CapCut template"
  description="Side-by-side: one-photo AI ceiling-fan outfit change vs CapCut multi-clip templates — time, skill, safety, copyright (Oct 2026)."
  canonicalPath="/blog/ceiling-fan-transition-vs-capcut/"
  ogType="article"
>
  <article class="section wrap prose">
    <p class="meta">Published 2026-10-22 · Updated 2026-10-23 · ~10 min</p>
    <h1>Ceiling Fan Transition AI vs CapCut template</h1>
    <p>
      Creators searching “ceiling fan transition” usually want an outfit-change wipe timed to a spinning-fan cut.
      Historically many tutorials used <strong>real phones on real fans</strong> — which is unsafe.
      Our template is <strong>AI-only</strong>: 1 photo → ~12–15s vertical. CapCut remains a strong DIY editor path.
      CapCut is a trademark of its respective owner; we are not affiliated.
    </p>

    <div class="callout warn">
      <strong>Safety:</strong> Never strap a phone (or camera) to a spinning ceiling fan. Use AI or safe filmed techniques that do not risk injury.
    </div>

    <h2>Feature matrix (as of Oct 2026)</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Feature</th>
            <th>Ceiling Fan on Viral Templates</th>
            <th>CapCut template / timeline path</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Primary input</strong></td>
            <td>1 photo → Generate</td>
            <td>Often 2+ clips or replaceable slots + keyframes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Editing skill</strong></td>
            <td>Minimal (consent + upload)</td>
            <td>Low–medium (cut on fan blade, match motion)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Typical length</strong></td>
            <td>~12–15s product target</td>
            <td>Template-defined; user can retime</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Physical fan required?</strong></td>
            <td><strong>No</strong> (AI wipe)</td>
            <td>Only if you film a real transition yourself</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Monetization</strong></td>
            <td>Credits / one-shot (from ${SITE.pricing.oneShotUsd})</td>
            <td>Free tier + CapCut Pro / export rules per vendor</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Music</strong></td>
            <td>No song license from us</td>
            <td>CapCut library + CapCut ToS</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Brand affiliation</strong></td>
            <td>None with CapCut / fan brands</td>
            <td>CapCut product</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Refund on failed AI job</strong></td>
            <td>Yes (credit)</td>
            <td>N/A</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Photo retention</strong></td>
            <td>~{SITE.photoRetentionDays} days</td>
            <td>Per CapCut privacy policy</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted)">
      CapCut pricing and export watermarks change; confirm on CapCut’s official pricing/help pages on the day you decide.
      Comparison written <strong>2026-10-23</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>When each wins</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Choose this AI template</strong> if you have one good full-body photo, want speed, and refuse physical fan stunts.</li>
      <li><strong>Choose CapCut</strong> if you already shoot multiple outfits on camera, need frame-level control, or rely on CapCut’s music library under their terms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How-to (AI path)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <a href={pathFor('en', '/create/ceiling-fan/')}>/create/ceiling-fan/</a>.</li>
      <li>Upload one adult-consent photo (full body preferred).</li>
      <li>Confirm consent <em>and</em> that you will not attempt a real-fan phone stunt.</li>
      <li>Generate (1 credit). Configure <code>FAL_*</code> for real renders; demo mode works without keys.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Related reading</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={pathFor('en', '/blog/what-is-bby-wow-ai/')}>What is Bby Wow AI?</a></li>
      <li><a href={pathFor('en', '/blog/how-to-make-kiss-cam-from-two-photos/')}>Kiss Cam from two photos</a></li>
      <li><a href={pathFor('en', '/faq/')}>FAQ comparison table</a></li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin-top:2rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={pathFor('en', '/create/ceiling-fan/')}>Create Ceiling Fan</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
